L("E088", "Law 41.3 (the match ball) and 41.4-41.5 (distraction): (1) a fielder may polish or dry the ball on his/her clothing or with a cloth 'that has been approved by the umpires'; (2) ball condition: 'deterioration ... greater than is consistent with the use it has received' becomes 'the condition of the ball has been unfairly changed', and the umpires must ask the opposing captain whether he/she wants a replacement ball (comparable wear), a repeat offence counting 'in the match by that team' rather than 'in that innings', with the bowler suspended-type sanctions repeated; (3) distraction: 5 Penalty runs are awarded to the batting side at the first deliberate distraction, 'the ball shall not count as one of the over', and fake fielding is added to the offence ('distract, deceive or obstruct' / 'distraction, deception or obstruction'); (4) reports go to the 'offending side'; gender-neutral wording.",
  UN, "no_cause_stated", "low", "none", "BOP/NZC list 'Match Ball: Any cloth used for drying a ball must be approved by the umpire(s)' among the 2017 major changes (S05) without a reason; the other changes in this 16-record event (replacement-ball procedure, penalty runs for distraction, 'deceive'/'deception') are real 2017 rule changes for which no source found states a reason.", ["S05", "S06"], date=D17, sec=ST, secsub="reorganisation")
