L("E091", "Law 41.16 (Non-striker leaving the wicket early) and warning provisions: the umpire informs the non-striker and each incoming batsman of a warning; if the bowler has not entered his/her delivery stride the umpire immediately calls Dead ball, otherwise waits until the ball is dead.",
  EN, "fairness_spirit", "low", "attributed", "S06 carries MCC's summary of the 2017 non-striker change: 'it is the batsman who is attempting to gain an advantage' and 'stay within your ground until the bowler has released the ball'. The attribution is to MCC as relayed by ThePapare, not checked against an MCC document.", ["S06", "S05"], date=D17, note="Provisions on warnings restated alongside.")
reorg("E092", "Law 41: the heading 'Batsman stealing a run' is dropped; the umpires jointly report offences and penalties are applied to 'the offending side'.")
pol("E093", "Law 41: for a second or subsequent offence of unfair action by a side, the bowler's end umpire awards 5 Penalty runs to the opposing side and the umpires together report the incident (previously 'additionally award 5 penalty runs to the fielding side').", ev=["S02"])
L("E094", "New Law 42 'Players' conduct': the umpires act on any unacceptable conduct; four levels of offence with escalating sanctions (warnings and 5 Penalty runs; suspension from the field for part of an innings; removal for the rest of the match).",
  EN, "fairness_spirit", "medium", "attributed", "ThePapare (S06) relays MCC's summary that the Code gives umpires 'appropriate on-field sanctions to deal with deteriorating levels of behaviour' (the opening words of the S06 sentence could not be confirmed verbatim); the 2017 guiding objectives include 'to give umpires more mechanisms to address instances of poor behaviour by players' (S02).",
  ["S06", "S02", "S05"], date=D17)
L("E095", "Law 5 (The bat) rewritten for 2017: the handle is made principally of cane and/or wood; solid material may be inserted into the blade; contact between the ball and the bat's parts; new limits on edge thickness and overall depth (Appendix B: depth 2.64 in/6.7 cm, edges 1.56 in/4.0 cm, bat gauge).",
  EN, "bowler_batsman_balance", "low", "inferred", "One of the 2017 Code's guiding objectives was 'to maintain a fair balance between bat and ball' (S02 l.21-22), and the new depth/edge limits are the part of the rewrite that bears on that balance; the preface does not tie the limits to the objective explicitly, and Cricbuzz's phrase 'redress the balance between bat and ball' (S06) is the journalist's own wording, not an MCC quotation.",
  ["S02", "S06"], date=D17, sec=ST, secsub="reorganisation", integrity="suspect")
L("E096", "Law 5: grip and covering provisions point to Appendix B ('the upper portion of the handle may be covered with a grip as defined in Appendix B.2.2'); blade covering, size and specifications cross-referenced.", ST, "reorganisation", "medium", "inferred", RE, ["S02"], date=D17)
conseq("E098", "Law 5: Type C cloth-covering paragraph removed and cross-references renumbered following the new bat Law and Appendix B.")
pol("E099", "Law 6 (The pitch): if the pitch is next to an artificial pitch closer than 5 ft/1.52 m from the middle stumps, the pitch on that side extends only to the junction; 'Description' and junior-cricket headings.", ev=["S02"])
conseq("E101", "Law 7 (The creases): 'The positions of a bowling crease, a popping crease and two return creases shall be marked by white lines, as set out in 7.2, 7.3 and 7.4'.")
L("E102", "Law 8 (The wickets): 'Description, width and pitching'; wickets pitched 'in the centres of the bowling creases' (replacing 'at a distance of 22 yards between the centres of the two middle stumps'); specifications re-set; AND new 8.3.4: 'Devices aimed at protecting player safety by limiting the distance that a bail can travel off the stumps will be allowed' (tethered bails).",
  EF, "medical_safety", "medium", "stated", "The Law text itself (8.3.4, 2017) states the purpose: protecting player safety by limiting how far a bail can travel. ThePapare (S06) adds, in its own words rather than MCC's, that tethered bails were permitted to help prevent injuries 'like the one suffered by South Africa's Mark Boucher in 2012 who was partially blinded by a flying bail'.",
  ["S02", "S06"], date=D17, sec=ST, secsub="reorganisation", note="The rest of the event is the re-setting of the wicket specifications.")
conseq("E103", "Law 9 (Preparation and maintenance of the playing area): rolling cross-references become '9.1.1 and 9.1.2'.")
reorg("E104", "Law 9: the rolling-delay clause: the insufficient-time provision for a late declaration is removed from this sub-clause (a removal, not only a renumbering).")
L("E105", "Law 9: clearance of debris and rolling cross-references renumbered ('9.2.1'); the 'Insufficient time to complete rolling' provision of the 2010 text is no longer in the 2017 text.", ST, "reorganisation", "medium", "inferred", RE, ["S02"], date=D17, sec=UN, secsub="no_cause_stated")
